body:
About this possibility for specifying the excitations: after discussing with @Cryoris we believe that this is probably the best way to go about introducing flexibility in terms of method variants like what we used to have through the `method_singles` and `method_doubles` parameters. You would then simply have different implementations of the method in this file: https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-nature/blob/35fb89c3a579796bf625e8c5dec72a3e1911ee80/qiskit_nature/components/variational_forms/excitation_op_builder.py

While writing this I actually noticed that I did not update that file after the aforementioned discussion. I had originally planned the excitation operator builders as very simple classes rather than standalone functions. I am open for either option but we should discuss what we prefer here. The docstring above kind-of assumes the latter.

@woodsp-ibm @pbark @stefan-woerner please comment :slightly_smiling_face:
